  "title": "Erdős Problem #14",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $A\\subseteq \\mathbb{N}$. Let $B\\subseteq \\mathbb{N}$ be the set of integers which are representable in exactly one way as the sum of two elements from $A$.\nIs it true that for all $\\epsilon>0$ and large $N$ $ \\lvert \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\backslash B\\rvert \\gg_\\epsilon N^{1/2-\\epsilon}? $ Is it possible that $ \\lvert \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\backslash B\\rvert =o(N^{1/2})? $ ",
